      "title": "From George Brown [before 1868]1",
      "header_text": [
        "From George Brown [before 1868]1[Down.]"
      ],
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "body_paragraph": 1,
          "text": "[Mr. G. Brown, of the Cirencester Agricultural College, who has particularly attended to the dentition of our domestic animals, writes to me that he has “several times noticed eight permanent incisors instead of six in the jaw.”]",
          "html_class": "",
          "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"
        }
      ],
      "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [],
      "body_container_count": 1,
      "used_whole_body_fallback": false,
      "editorial_summary": "Summary Has “several times noticed eight permanent incisors instead of six in the jaw [of the horse]”.",
      "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1The date is established by the publication of this fragment in Variation 1: 50; Variation was published early in 1868 (see Correspondence vol. 16).2Brown’s correspondence with CD has not been found in the Darwin Archive–CUL.",
      "letter_container_present": true
    },
